{% set design %}
<section class="docs-section">
  <h2 id="d-usage">Usage</h2>
  <p>Lists are the workhorse content component — mail, contacts, settings,
     files. Flint's list follows the Gmail-2020 spec: fixed-height rows with a
     leading zone (24px icon or 40px avatar), a text block, and a trailing
     meta zone. Rows separate by spacing, not rules.</p>
  <h3>Do use it when</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Content is a <strong>collection of peer items</strong> — messages,
        people, documents, settings.</li>
    <li>Rows repeat the same structure with varying text and metadata.</li>
    <li>You want selectable rows that fit a shell (selected rows take the tint
        fill, like Gmail's mail list).</li>
  </ul>
  <h3>Don't use it when</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Items are heterogeneous content blocks — use cards.</li>
    <li>Rows need to expand/collapse (accordions) — not in the library yet.</li>
    <li>You need multi-select checkboxes — planned; the current meta zone holds
        one control, but selection is single via <code>aria-current</code>.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

